# =============================================================================
# E3-DoH Reproducibility — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
#
# Chapter 5 of the thesis: E3-DoH (Enhanced Evolutionary Encryption for
# Multi-Protocol DNS Security — DoH, DoT, DoQ).
#
# This file is deliberately permissive about what is ignored. The artifact
# is intended to be checked out by a reviewer who runs it on their own
# hardware; nothing that is a byproduct of a run should end up in the
# repository. The two exceptions are documented explicitly at the bottom of
# each relevant section:
#
#   - configs/*.yaml    : configuration is committed, not ignored
#   - expected_outputs/ : reference outputs are committed, not ignored
#
# Everything that a run produces goes into one of the following directories,
# all of which are ignored:
#
#   data/raw/           : downloaded datasets (40 GB; never committed)
#   data/processed/     : feature store produced by preprocess scripts
#   outputs/            : fresh runs (tables, figures, logs)
#   logs/               : structured JSON logs
#   .cache/             : intermediate caches (numba, torch, HF, etc.)
#   artifacts/          : attack simulation PCAPs and namespace state
#
# =============================================================================


